{%- comment -%}
  "Chris Shi" as single-stroke cursive, for the signature intro on the
  portfolio index. Letterforms are the public-domain Hershey Script Simplex
  face (Allen V. Hershey, US NBS), laid out and smoothed by local/sig/sig_gen.py:
  each word's letter strokes are chained into ONE continuous pen line (glyph
  exit bridged to the next entry, joins rounded by the smoothing pass), so a
  word draws without the pen ever lifting; the i-dots follow their word, the
  way a hand dots an i. Every path is resampled at even arc-length,
  Gaussian-smoothed (endpoints fixed) and fitted with Catmull-Rom, so the
  curves read as pen strokes rather than the font's integer-grid polylines.
  The underline flourish is hand-authored. Path order is writing order — the
  intro script draws each path in sequence by animating stroke-dashoffset.
{%- endcomment -%}
